From fcf1d736909780f56c17da11fbe6abaa2eb4bfa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:32:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): take over a chat open in another Hermes
 window [daveey]

A chat whose active-session lease a different LIVE process holds (e.g. a
second Desktop app whose SSH backend runs on this Mac) could never be
moved: every submit was refused SESSION_NOT_OWNED until that process let go.

- hermes_cli/active_sessions.py: take_over_active_session() replaces the
  live owner's registry entry under the same lock and strict read as
  try_acquire (unreadable registry fails closed), recording took_over_from
  / took_over_at; find_takeover_of(), acknowledge_takeover() and
  takeover_acknowledged() (acked, or the old pid is dead).
- New RPC session.take_over (methods_session_takeover.py, long handler):
  in-process detached sibling first, else the registry takeover; waits up
  to HERMES_SESSION_TAKEOVER_ACK_TIMEOUT_S (8s) for the old owner's ack,
  then reloads history from state.db. Refusal -> 4090 + reason.
- Revocation watcher (daemon, HERMES_SESSION_TAKEOVER_POLL_S=2s, stat-gated):
  a backend whose lease was taken over drops it (never the new owner's
  entry), marks _lease_taken_over, interrupts the turn, cancels open
  clarify/approval/sudo requests, emits an `error` event with
  error_surface SESSION_NOT_OWNED, and acknowledges. Its next submit
  re-claims and is refused SESSION_NOT_OWNED.
- ErrorPayload gains optional error_surface; contracts regenerated.
- Tests: registry takeover (real live foreign pid), watcher (idle, running
  turn, pending clarify), RPC (ack / timeout / already_owner / fail closed),
  and a two-process end-to-end.
